; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Honeycomb Tiles
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     hexagon, tiling, grid, coordinates, random
; SUMMARY:  Covers the screen with hexagon tiles like a honeycomb, some full of honey and some empty.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Hexagons fit together with no gaps, which is why bees use them.
;   This program lays hexagon tiles in columns, each column shifted
;   half a tile up, and paints most cells in shades of honey. Cells
;   near the middle are fuller, the ones at the edge are often empty.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Run it again for a different honeycomb.
;   Change SIDE to make the cells bigger or smaller.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * why hexagons tile: three 120 degree corners meet at each point
;   * where to put the center of each tile in a staggered grid
;   * using DISTANCE to make the middle of the picture different
;   * mixing two colors by a fraction
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make SIDE 15 for a fine honeycomb.
;   * Try squares or triangles instead. Do they tile too? Pentagons?
;   * Paint the cells in rainbow colors by column.
; ============================================================

make "side 34

; A flat-topped hexagon with its center at (x, y). We start at the
; left corner and walk round with right turns of 60 degrees.
to hexagon :x :y :color
  penup setxy :x - :side :y setheading 30 pendown
  filled :color [repeat 6 [forward :side right 60]]
end

; Mix two colors: fraction 0 gives the first, 1 gives the second.
to mix :a :b :fraction
  output (map [int ?1 + :fraction * (?2 - ?1)] :a :b)
end

; Pick a cell's color. The closer it is to the middle of the screen,
; the more likely it is to be full of honey, and the darker the honey.
to cellcolor :x :y
  localmake "far (sqrt :x * :x + :y * :y) / 420
  if (random 100) < 100 * :far [output [250 240 210]]        ; empty wax
  output mix [255 215 60] [200 110 10] (1 - :far) * (random 100) / 100
end

; Columns are 1.5 sides apart. Every other column is pushed up by
; half a tile so its hexagons slot in between those next to it.
to honeycomb
  localmake "h :side * sqrt 3
  for [col -9 9] [
    localmake "x 1.5 * :side * :col
    localmake "shift ifelse 0 = remainder abs :col 2 [0] [:h / 2]
    for [row -5 5] [
      localmake "y :h * :row + :shift
      hexagon :x :y cellcolor :x :y
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [120 80 30]
setpensize 4
setpencolor [150 100 30]
honeycomb
